    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.test\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nI was setting up some tests for my plugin function which works asynchronously with the help of lua coroutines. I try to implement a demo test with plenary.nvim because I thought that my asynchronous module could causing problem and found out that plenary.nvim output logs are also not show in the `stdout` when running `mini.test` in headless mode.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n```lua\nlocal test = require(\"mini.test\")\nlocal T = test.new_set()\n\nT[\"can build tree\"] = function()\n  local a = require(\"plenary.async\")\n  a.void(function()\n    print(\"hello\")\n    vim.print(a.uv.fs_stat(\"/path/to/somewhere\"))\n    print(\"bye\")\n  end)()\nend\n\nreturn T\n```\n<img width=\"482\" height=\"356\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c4316a0b-ed5b-42ae-bba5-8e55ba97f968\" />\n\nExpected output should be \"hello\" then file stats and at the end \"bye\" but i am getting \"hello\" only.",
