            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is similar to #1863 and has the same resolution as described in [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/1863#issuecomment-2983629024).\n\nHere is one way to have this tested:\n\n```lua\nlocal test = require('mini.test')\n\nlocal child = test.new_child_neovim()\nlocal eq = test.expect.equality\n\nlocal T = test.new_set({\n  hooks = {\n    pre_case = function()\n      -- Make sure to set up child process in a way that has available the\n      -- tested async functionality. Here it is 'plenary.nvim' installed in one\n      -- of the '~/.local/share/nvim/site/pack/<your-name>/opt/plenary.nvim'.\n      -- If async feature comes from your plugin, make sure that child process\n      -- can load it.\n      --\n      -- One way to do it is to have `vim.cmd('let &rtp.=\",\".getcwd()')`.\n      child.restart()\n      child.cmd('let &packpath.=\",~/.local/share/nvim/site\"')\n      child.lua('vim.cmd(\"packadd plenary.nvim\")')\n    end,\n    post_once = child.stop,\n  },\n})\n\nT['can build tree'] = function()\n  child.lua([[\n    local a = require(\"plenary.async\")\n    a.void(function()\n      print(\"hello\")\n      vim.print(a.uv.fs_stat(\"/path/to/somewhere\"))\n      print(\"bye\")\n    end)()\n  ]])\n\n  -- Wait for a small amount of time *in the outer process* for async\n  -- actions to finish *in the child neovim process*.\n  vim.uv.sleep(10)\n\n  -- Check printed messages. Which in this case returns an string:\n  eq(child.cmd_capture('messages'), 'hello\\nENOENT: no such file or directory: /path/to/somewhere\\nbye')\nend\n\nreturn T\n```\n\nClosing as \"working as expected\".",
