            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ... i understand that it is not possible to dynamically block neovim from exit before async task get completed.\n\nIt is possible with `vim.wait` inside child process, but it usually more of a hassle. Here is an example:\n\n```lua\nT['can wait'] = function()\n  child.lua([[\n    local a = require(\"plenary.async\")\n    local done = false\n    a.void(function()\n      print(\"hello\")\n      vim.defer_fn(function()\n        print('Wow')\n        done = true\n      end, 50)\n      print(\"bye\")\n    end)()\n    vim.wait(100, function() return done end)\n  ]])\n\n  -- Check printed messages. Which in this case returns an string:\n  eq(child.cmd_capture('messages'), 'hello\\nbye\\nWow')\nend\n```",
